  "description": "AFABES crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C138 H141 Cd6 N6 Nd5 O63 S3. From the CIF bond table, Nd1 (Nd) has 8 O neighbors; Nd2 (Nd) has 8 O neighbors; Nd3 (Nd) has 8 O neighbors; Nd4 (Nd) has 9 O neighbors; Nd5 (Nd) has 9 O neighbors; Cd1 (Cd) has 6 O neighbors; Cd2 (Cd) has 7 O neighbors; Cd3 (Cd) has 6 O neighbors; Cd4 (Cd) has 7 O neighbors; Cd5 (Cd) has 6 O neighbors; Cd6 (Cd) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 13 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.531-3.878 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 95.57-109.98°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Cd6Nd5(L)3(L′)6(OH)3(OAc)15] (C138H137Cd6N6O63S3Nd5; CCDC C138H141Cd6N6Nd5O63S3). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 3 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 15 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article formula). Article name explicitly identifies I(I), I(II).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
